      "title": "GitLab CI: Have the Commit Check pre-commit run on the first commit",
      "message": "GitLab CI: Have the Commit Check pre-commit run on the first commit\n\nThe pre-commit tool, as a hook, expects to run *before* a commit\nhappens, so it compares HEAD to the working tree/index. When run\nafter a commit, it expects to be passed the ancestor of the new\ncommit, i.e. HEAD~ not HEAD.\n\nIt also always checked multiple commits, but produced a single output\nresult for the collective total of commits instead of splitting them.\nAs it is now, passing in several commits ends up producing reports\nthat are subsets of each other (by comparing each commit to the current\ntree/HEAD, instead of comparing each commit to its immediate parent.)\n\nSo currently the Commit Check is not running the pre-commit on the\nfirst commit of a MR (which means that it's not running it at all\nin the typical case of a 1 commit MR.)\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
